@page "/about"
<PageTitle>About · Mars Survival Handbook</PageTitle>
<div class="page"><div class="wrap">
    <h1>About<br />the mission</h1>
    <p class="lead">Mars Survival Handbook answers NASA Space Apps 2026: <b>Interplanetary Survival Guide – Martian Map</b>. Team Road to NASA, Space Apps Ho Chi Minh City.</p>
    <div class="list">
        <div class="item"><span class="idx">01</span><div><h3>How the planner works</h3><p>Place a habitat and draw an EVA route. Distances use Mars' radius of 3,389.5 km. Time is distance over walking speed plus science stops; the verdict compares it with suit life and a safety reserve. All values are adjustable planning assumptions, not flight rules.</p></div></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="idx">02</span><div><h3>Data and credits</h3><p>Basemaps: NASA/JPL Mars Trek (MOLA elevation, Viking mosaic). Mission context: public NASA mission pages. Map engine: Leaflet. Knowledge content: our own backend API.</p></div></div>
        <div class="item"><span class="idx">03</span><div><h3>AI use</h3><p>Parts of this code were written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic). Team members reviewed it and are responsible for the result.</p></div></div>
    </div>
</div></div>
